  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A particle of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> and charge <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q\"></span> enters a uniform magnetic field of strength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span> and moves on a circular path with speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>. The angle between the particle’s path and the direction of the magnetic field is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span>. Initially, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta = 45^{o}\"></span>. What changes will definitely increase the radius of the particle’s path?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">Increasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> and increasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60^{o}\"></span>.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">Decreasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> and decreasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q\"></span>.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">Increasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> and decreasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span>.</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">Decreasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span> and decreasing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30^{o}\"></span>.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
